title: 'delete_ref cannot fail: error discarded, WRITES incremented regardless'
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`lib/App/karr/Git.pm:273-279`:

    try { $repo->reference_delete($ref) };   # no catch, error discarded
    $WRITES++;
    return 1;

Always reports success, and always increments the `$WRITES` gate that
`SyncGuard`/`flush_armed` use to decide whether a push is needed — even when
nothing was deleted.

Reported as low because the auditor could not construct a case where this alone
causes user-visible damage. It is on the list because it is exactly the shape of
the already-fixed #31 (a return value that can only say yes), it feeds the push
decision of the insurance guard, and it will be someone's confusing afternoon
the first time a delete quietly does nothing.

Fix: catch the error, return false on failure, and only count a write that
happened.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
